osingRange":null},{"range":[21,8,12],"TypedRange":null,"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/Box#__init__().(self)","symbol_roles":8,"TypedEnclosingRange":null},{"range":[21,13,14],"TypedRange":null,"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/Box#n.","symbol_roles":1,"TypedEnclosingRange":null},{"range":[21,17,18],"TypedRange":null,"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/Box#__init__().(n)","symbol_roles":8,"TypedEnclosingRange":null}],"symbols":[{"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/__init__:","documentation":["(module) ctx"]},{"symbol":"local 0","documentation":["```python\n(module) t\n```","---\n","The typing module: Support for gradual typing as defined by PEP 484 and subsequent PEPs.\n\nAmong other things, the module includes the following:\n * Generic, Protocol, and internal machinery to support generic aliases.\nAll subscripted types like X\\[int\\], Union\\[int, str\\] are generic aliases.\n * Various \"special forms\" that have unique meanings in type annotations:\nAny, Never, ClassVar, Self, Concatenate, Unpack, and others.\n * Classes whose instances can be type arguments to generic classes and functions:\nTypeVar, ParamSpec, TypeVarTuple.\n * Public helper functions: get\\_type\\_hints, overload, cast, final, and others.\n * Several protocols to support duck-typing:\nSupportsFloat, SupportsIndex, SupportsAbs, and others.\n * Special types: NewType, NamedTuple, TypedDict.\n * Deprecated aliases for builtin types and collections.abc ABCs.\n\nAny name not present in \\_\\_all\\_\\_ is an implementation detail\nthat may be changed without notice. Use at your own risk!"]},{"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/current().","documentation":["```python\n@t.overload\ndef current(\n  silent: t.Literal[False] = False\n) -> int:\n```"]},{"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/current().(silent)"},{"symbol":"scip-python python repo 0 ctx/current().","documentation":["```python\n@t.overload\ndef current(\n  silent: bool = ...\n) -> int | None:\n```"]},{"symbol":"s